  "notes": "Proposed in architecture Amendment 1 (docs/architecture/SessionTurn-Review-AgentContext-Architecture-Amendment-1-Durable-HV.md, section 19.1); plan PLAN-HVPIPELINE-001, not approved; created 2026-10-16 so the requirement is captured as it emerges.",
  "status": "pending",
  "acceptanceCriteria": [
    {
      "id": "AC001",
      "text": "Given options missing one of the five reviewers, naming an unknown or duplicate reviewer, an unknown strategy, or an enabled Copilot reviewer without a configured model (section 10), when the server starts, then startup fails naming the entry (`HostileValidationOptionsMissingUnknownOrDuplicateReviewerFailsStartup`).",
      "isSatisfied": false
    },
    {
      "id": "AC002",
      "text": "Given a fresh workspace, when the server starts, then five `HvReviewer` rows exist `Unverified`, and a second start does not overwrite a row changed through the API (`ReviewerSeedingInsertsFiveOnceNeverOverwrites`).",
      "isSatisfied": false
    },
    {
      "id": "AC003",
      "text": "Given a reviewer with no configured effort, and a reviewer other than Copilot with no configured model, when its launch is built, then the effort is the highest its CLI accepts (Codex `max`, Claude `max`, Cline `xhigh`, Grok `xhigh`, Copilot `max`; VI-08), never a lower or a refused value, and the model is the CLI default recorded from provenance (`ReviewerAdapterDefaultsToHighestEffortAndCliDefaultModel`).",
      "isSatisfied": false
    },
    {
      "id": "AC004",
      "text": "Given an update with a stale `expectedStateVersion`, when it is applied, then 409 `conflict` with `retryable: false` and `details.field` `expectedStateVersion` and nothing changes (`UpdateReviewerStaleStateVersion409NothingChanged`).",
      "isSatisfied": false
    },
    {
      "id": "AC005",
      "text": "Given an update that changes the strategy, agent path, model, or effort, when it commits, then the reviewer is `Unverified` with reason `configuration_changed` and `reviewer_unverified` is appended (`UpdateReviewerLaunchChangeMakesUnverifiedAndNotifies`).",
      "isSatisfied": false
    },
    {
      "id": "AC006",
      "text": "Given the REST, MCP, client, REPL, and Director surfaces, when each lists, gets, and updates a reviewer, then each returns the same record and the same error codes (`ReviewerSurfacesParityGoldenContract`).",
      "isSatisfied": false
    }
  ],
  "description": "Reviewer pool configuration and real-time management. Sources: S-02, R-08. Use cases: UC-HV-01.",
