      "CreatedUtc": "2026-10-16T22:48:12Z",
      "Path": "plugins/core/lib-ps/plugin-hook.ps1",
      "Line": 1065,
      "Commit": "6dbc384323c036a57c37fd9eaf2259879c1d956f",
      "Body": "**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Return a proof shape that the stop hook can consume**\n\nWhen a cached session is stale, this production REPL call cannot produce the proof consumed below: the added client method returns `Task<UnifiedSessionLogDto>`, which is absent from `GenericClientPassthrough.AwaitTaskResultAsync` and therefore raises `Unsupported task result type`; even after adding that case, `UnifiedSessionLogDto` contains `status` and `turns`, not the expected `workspacePath`, `requestId`, `outcome`, or `serverStatus`. The catch consequently treats completed persisted turns as active, leaving the stop gate blocked indefinitely; expose a matching proof DTO or derive the requested turn outcome from the returned session DTO.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\n<!-- codex-code-review-finding:v1 -->",
      "Url": "https://github.com/sharpninja/McpServer/pull/81#discussion_r4300020832"
    },
    {
      "Id": 4300020839,
      "ReviewId": 5554472359,
      "CreatedUtc": "2026-10-16T22:48:12Z",
      "Path": "src/QBrainAi.Client/WorkspacePathNormalizer.cs",
      "Line": 130,
      "Commit": "6dbc384323c036a57c37fd9eaf2259879c1d956f",
      "Body": "**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Treat root-relative Windows segments as rooted**\n\nOn a Windows host, a segment such as `\\repo` is rooted and must replace the path after retaining the current drive, but `IsWindowsRooted` recognizes only drive-qualified and UNC paths. `Combine(\"C:/content\", \"\\\\repo\")` therefore returns `C:/content/repo` instead of `C:/repo`; in particular, `ResolveRepoRootWorkspacePath` now resolves a root-relative `RepoRoot` under the content directory and selects the wrong workspace and tenant. Handle a leading backslash as Windows-root-relative using the root drive.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\n<!-- codex-code-review-finding:v1 -->",
      "Url": "https://github.com/sharpninja/McpServer/pull/81#discussion_r4300020839"
    },
    {
      "Id": 4300020846,
      "ReviewId": 5554472359,
      "CreatedUtc": "2026-10-16T22:48:12Z",
      "Path": "src/QBrainAi.Services/Services/FileGitHubWorkspaceTokenStore.cs",
      "Line": 326,
      "Commit": "6dbc384323c036a57c37fd9eaf2259879c1d956f",
      "Body": "**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Preserve access to legacy GitHub token entries**\n\nAfter upgrading on Windows, this changes the persistent token-store lookup key from the prior `C:\\repo` form to `C:/repo`, but entries already stored in the JSON document are never canonicalized on read. The `OrdinalIgnoreCase` comparisons in `GetAsync`, `UpsertAsync`, and `DeleteAsync` do not equate different separators, so existing GitHub credentials become inaccessible, an upsert creates a duplicate entry, and deletion leaves the legacy secret behind. Normalize loaded entry paths or migrate the token document before using the new key format.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\n<!-- codex-code-review-finding:v1 -->",
      "Url": "https://github.com/sharpninja/McpServer/pull/81#discussion_r4300020846"
    },
    {
      "Id": 4300020851,
      "ReviewId": 5554472359,
      "CreatedUtc": "2026-10-16T22:48:12Z",
      "Path": "plugins/core/lib-ps/repl-invoke.ps1",
      "Line": 738,
      "Commit": "6dbc384323c036a57c37fd9eaf2259879c1d956f",
      "Body": "**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Keep descendants killable after the root process exits**\n\nWhen the REPL wrapper starts a background descendant and then exits before the deadline, `HasExited` is already true here, so `Kill(true)` is skipped even if the descendant still owns stdout/stderr or continues running detached. The subsequent loop can only time out—or can report success once the pipes close—while leaving that descendant alive, defeating the bounded-child guarantee. Start the child in an owned process group/job and terminate that group independently of the root process's exit state.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\n<!-- codex-code-review-finding:v1 -->",
      "Url": "https://github.com/sharpninja/McpServer/pull/81#discussion_r4300020851"
    },
